# CLI Models

This document describes the descriptor models used internally by the CLI framework.

## CliCommandDescriptor

**Location:** `Models/CliCommandDescriptor.cs`

Represents a discovered CLI command with all its metadata.

```csharp
namespace Cyrena.CLI.Models;

public sealed class CliCommandDescriptor
{
    public string Name { get; init; }
    public string? Description { get; init; }
    public MethodInfo Method { get; init; }
    public object? Target { get; init; }
    public IReadOnlyList<CliParameterDescriptor> Parameters { get; init; }
    public bool IsStatic { get; }
}
```

**Properties:**
- `Name`: The command name used in the CLI (e.g., "some-command")
- `Description`: Optional description from the `[CliCommand]` attribute
- `Method`: The reflection MethodInfo for the command handler
- `Target`: The instance that contains the command method (null for static methods)
- `Parameters`: List of parameter descriptors for this command
- `IsStatic`: Whether the command method is static

## CliParameterDescriptor

**Location:** `Models/CliParameterDescriptor.cs`

Represents a discovered CLI parameter with all its metadata.

```csharp
namespace Cyrena.CLI.Models;

public sealed class CliParameterDescriptor
{
    public string Name { get; init; }
    public Type ParameterType { get; init; }
    public ParameterInfo ParameterInfo { get; init; }
    public string? Description { get; init; }
    public bool Required { get; init; }
    public object? DefaultValue { get; init; }
    public bool IsMultiValue { get; init; }
}
```

**Properties:**
- `Name`: The parameter name (e.g., "name" for `--name`)
- `ParameterType`: The .NET type of the parameter
- `ParameterInfo`: The reflection ParameterInfo
- `Description`: Optional description from the `[CliParam]` attribute
- `Required`: Whether the parameter is required
- `DefaultValue`: Default value if parameter is not provided
- `IsMultiValue`: Whether the parameter accepts multiple values (arrays/lists)

## Usage

These models are primarily used internally by the CLI service but are exposed for:
- Introspection (listing available commands)
- Help generation
- Custom command routing
- Testing and validation

```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();

var commands = service.GetRegisteredCommands();
foreach (var cmd in commands)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Command: {cmd.Name}");
    Console.WriteLine($"  Description: {cmd.Description}");
    foreach (var param in cmd.Parameters)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"  --{param.Name}: {param.ParameterType.Name}");
    }
}
```
